1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:06,079
Who decides how close one satellite may
come to another?

2
00:00:07,029 --> 00:00:12,507
16 Oct: a Russian military satellite came
within 5 km of a Finnish company's satellite.

3
00:00:13,457 --> 00:00:18,936
Nothing collided. But no law or treaty
sets a minimum distance.

4
00:00:19,886 --> 00:00:25,364
The nearest rule: the 1967 Outer Space
Treaty asks for due regard.

5
00:00:26,214 --> 00:00:31,943
Within five kilometres. Legal minimum
distance: none.
